    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent core anchored by **Junior Caminero** (79.84) and **Yordan Alvarez** (72.94). **Junior Caminero** remains our premier start; despite a challenging left-handed matchup against Lopez, his xwOBA of 0.376 and a favorable park factor provide a massive ceiling. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a strong wind-out projection and a prime #2 hole placement against the right-handed Blade Tidwell, solidifying his status as an elite daily contributor. We are also leaning heavily on the platoon advantages of **Carson Benge** (61.23) and **Caleb Durbin** (60.77). **Carson Benge** is locked into the clean-up spot against Elder, though his potential is slightly tempered by a 37% rain risk that we will monitor closely as game time approaches.\n\nWhile the top of the order carries the heavy lifting, **Kyle Schwarber** (60.77) earns the utility spot due to the high-leverage opportunity of leading off against Dobbins. On the margins, **Christian Yelich** (58.30) narrowly missed the \"Strong\" start threshold but remains a viable play due to his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching, providing more reliability than the bench alternatives. Our most difficult decision revolved around the bottom of the order; while we lack depth on the bench today due to league-wide off-days for players like **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Colt Keith**, the decision to stick with **Gary Sanchez** (43.64) is purely a preservation play. With **Trea Turner** and **Kazuma Okamoto** unavailable, we are essentially forced into our current alignment, emphasizing the need for **Josh Smith** to maximize his +14% platoon edge against Gray to prevent a stall in our offensive efficiency.",
